From 1a4c3ff627ff16f8a708695522819d980f627151 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Liu Dongmiao <473522+liudongmiao@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 00:51:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/12] quic: pad ACK-only Initial datagrams with bytes outside
 any packet

When congestion limited, the TX packetiser uses the ACK_ONLY archetype,
which cannot add PADDING frames. A datagram with an Initial packet must
be at least 1200 bytes, so the datagram was abandoned after its ACK
frames were generated, and the ACK of an Initial packet was not sent
until the peer sent another ack-eliciting packet.

Pad such a datagram with zero bytes outside any packet, which RFC 9000
s. 14.1 allows and a receiver discards as an invalid packet. The ACK
goes out at once, and the ACK-only packets stay out of bytes in flight,
so the congestion window is respected (RFC 9002 s. 7). A 1-RTT packet
must end its datagram, so its ACK is sent in the next datagram.

A server needs to pad only a datagram with an ack-eliciting Initial
packet (RFC 9000 s. 14.1), so its ACK-only Initial packet is no longer
padded.

Add quic_txp_test scripts for an Initial ACK sent while congestion
limited, alone, with a Handshake ACK and with a 1-RTT ACK, and for the
padding of server datagrams.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 include/internal/quic_record_tx.h |  12 ++
 include/internal/quic_txp.h       |   1 +
 ssl/quic/quic_channel.c           |   1 +
 ssl/quic/quic_record_tx.c         |  12 ++
 ssl/quic/quic_txp.c               |  43 ++++--
 test/quic_txp_test.c              | 226 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 285 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/internal/quic_record_tx.h b/include/internal/quic_record_tx.h
index d983d8bc7928c..2430beb946472 100644
--- a/include/internal/quic_record_tx.h
+++ b/include/internal/quic_record_tx.h
@@ -242,6 +242,18 @@ int ossl_qtx_write_pkt(OSSL_QTX *qtx, const OSSL_QTX_PKT *pkt);
  */
 void ossl_qtx_finish_dgram(OSSL_QTX *qtx);
 
+/**
+ * @brief Pads the datagram being built with zero bytes after its packets.
+ *
+ * A receiver discards the padding as an invalid packet. Does nothing if the
+ * datagram holds no packet, is already at least min_len bytes long, or cannot
+ * hold min_len bytes.
+ *
+ * @param qtx      QTX instance.
+ * @param min_len  Length to pad the datagram to.
+ */
+void ossl_qtx_pad_dgram(OSSL_QTX *qtx, size_t min_len);
+
 /*
  * (Attempt to) flush any datagrams which are queued for transmission. Note that
  * this does not cancel coalescing; call ossl_qtx_finish_dgram() first if that
diff --git a/include/internal/quic_txp.h b/include/internal/quic_txp.h
