From 993fddac29af4ae5a3eeb5649387d50c8994a6fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Liu Dongmiao <473522+liudongmiao@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:28:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] quic: resend unacknowledged data in PTO probes

An Initial PTO probe resent CRYPTO data only until the Handshake keys
were available, so a server never resent a lost ServerHello in it. A
Handshake PTO probe, or a 1-RTT PTO probe with no new data to send,
carried only PING. Lost data was then not resent until an ACK showed it
lost. A lost ServerHello or client Finished stalled the handshake, and a
lost request or response stalled its stream. A lost HANDSHAKE_DONE kept
the client from confirming the handshake, so it could not set a 1-RTT
PTO timer (RFC 9002 s. 6.2.1) and kept probing with Handshake packets,
which the server ignores once it has discarded the Handshake keys.

Resend Initial CRYPTO data after the Handshake keys are available too.
If Handshake data is queued, the first Initial probe gives way to it,
and the second resends the Initial data, which may hold a lost
ServerHello. In a Handshake probe, resend the first unacknowledged
Handshake CRYPTO data. A datagram with an Initial packet may be padded,
so a Handshake probe in such a datagram waits for anti-amplification
credit for a full datagram. Otherwise the probe is shrunk to fit the
remaining credit.

In a 1-RTT probe, when no stream has data it can send now, pick the
lowest-ID stream whose sent data or FIN is still unacknowledged. Requeue
its first unacknowledged data, as much as fits in the probe, or its FIN
alone. Also resend HANDSHAKE_DONE until a copy of it is acknowledged,
and do not regenerate a lost copy after that.

Add quic_txp_test scripts for Handshake probes with CRYPTO data in
flight, with new CRYPTO data queued, and with too little
anti-amplification credit, and for an Initial probe with more Handshake
data queued than fits in one datagram. Add scripts for 1-RTT probes that
resend STREAM data, a FIN or HANDSHAKE_DONE, for 1-RTT probes that must
not resend them, and for a lost copy of HANDSHAKE_DONE after another
copy is acknowledged. The Initial PTO script with Handshake data queued
now expects the second probe to resend the Initial data.

